# DECISIONS.log — append-only
# Every model must append here before making any meaningful change.
# Format: YYYY-MM-DD | decision | reason
# Entries before 2026-07-19 are reconstructed from code evidence on the uncommitted `restructure` branch; dates are approximate (migration file dated 2026-07-18).

2026-07-18 | Rebuilt site as operational platform; deleted per-page section components for shared PublicPage kit | ~45 routes need one visual system; per-page components caused drift (inferred)
2026-07-18 | Adopted "Warm Sky Editorial" rebrand: navy/teal/pink/action palette, Gabarito + Newsreader fonts | New brand direction from claude.ai/design mocks
2026-07-18 | Kept Chakra UI v3 as the component/styling layer; tokens centralized in src/lib/theme.ts | Existing investment; v3 recipes cover theming needs
2026-07-18 | All operational features gated by env-readiness functions (lib/env.ts), failing closed to EmptyState/503 | Ship the site before Supabase/Resend/Paystack/Turnstile are provisioned without ever accepting data that can't be handled
2026-07-18 | Standardized intake API pipeline: honeypot → hashed-IP rate limit → Turnstile → Zod → service-role insert → email + outbox | Uniform spam/abuse defense and auditable email delivery for health-adjacent data
2026-07-18 | Three Supabase clients (browser anon / SSR cookie / server-only service-role), all null when unconfigured | Keep service-role out of client bundles; support fail-closed gates
2026-07-18 | Admin console requires Supabase session + MFA aal2 + active staff_profiles row; 7-role static permission map | Staff handle sensitive case data; defense in depth ahead of feature build-out
2026-07-18 | Donations: Paystack initialize + signature-verified webhook is the only path to "confirmed"; amounts in NGN minor units | Never trust client-side payment callbacks
2026-07-18 | Forms are uncontrolled FormData → JSON → /api, server-side Zod is the single validator; no form library | Minimal dependencies; one validation source (inferred)
2026-07-18 | Added scripts/check-content.mjs to CI: blocks fake phone numbers, unverified events/prices/claims, placeholder bank accounts, dead legacy routes | Charity credibility requires no invented facts; prior site had unverified content
2026-07-18 | Removed unverified content (walk promo, fake pricing, legacy patient/donor routes); replaced with honest EmptyState surfaces | Trust posture: only verified information is published
2026-07-18 | Legal/policy pages driven by data in src/content/policies.ts; legacy URLs redirect to /policies/* | Single copy source; preserve inbound links
2026-07-18 | Quality gate npm run check = lint + typecheck + vitest + content check + build; Playwright asserts fail-closed behavior | One command defines "done"
2026-07-19 | Chakra theme tokens are the ONLY styling mechanism; Tailwind, cn()/clsx/tailwind-merge, react-icons, next-themes forbidden and slated for removal | Owner decision — prevent style drift from unused installed deps
2026-07-19 | The restructure branch working tree is the canonical project state despite being uncommitted | Owner confirmation during governance-doc onboarding
2026-07-19 | Added governance docs (AGENTS.md, DESIGN_SPEC.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, PLAN.md, CONVENTIONS.md, DECISIONS.log); CLAUDE.md rewritten to defer to AGENTS.md | Give any model/developer a zero-memory onboarding path
2026-07-19 | Nav restructure: 8-item primary header nav (desktop at xl, Donate pill always visible), Chakra v3 Drawer mobile menu, shared src/lib/navigation.ts, footer regrouped Explore/Get Involved/Trust & Legal | Kill link drift between Header/Footer; drawer gains focus trap + scroll lock for free
2026-07-19 | Added a tightly cropped display-only wordmark with responsive header and footer sizing | Remove transparent canvas that made the visible brand too small while preserving the original metadata and social asset
2026-08-02 | Header nav reduced to 4 grouped dropdowns (About, Get Support, Learn, Get Involved) + Contact + Donate; Chakra v3 Menu on desktop and Accordion in the mobile drawer; desktop breakpoint xl -> lg; footer regrouped to mirror the same five columns | A flat 7-link row forced the hamburger onto every tablet/small laptop and buried /about/founder-story, /support/request, /case-status and /events
2026-08-02 | Added an explicit "Home" text link as the leftmost primary-nav item (desktop) and top of the mobile drawer, exported as a standalone homeLink rather than joining navGroups/standaloneNavLinks; footer left unchanged | Many visitors do not know the logo returns home; homeLink stays separate because footerGroups is derived by positional destructuring of navGroups and spreads standaloneNavLinks, so either would have silently reshaped the footer
2026-08-02 | client/ is now a strictly front-end application: deleted Supabase (all three clients + migration), the six /api route handlers, the admin console, all forms, Resend email, Paystack, Turnstile, the Supabase-RPC rate limiter, and lib/env.ts readiness gating (siteUrl() survives) | Owner decision — the operational service will be rebuilt later in a separate top-level server/ folder; every gated surface was already dark in practice, so the code was unreachable weight. Recoverable from git at cacf25b
2026-08-02 | Backend-dependent actions are now non-navigating "Coming soon" markers (ComingSoonTag/ComingSoonPanel/ComingSoonAction in components/common/PublicPage.tsx) instead of links to fail-closed pages | A CTA that navigates only to "not configured" wastes the click; the marker states the truth in place. ComingSoonAction is a styled span, not a disabled button, because the theme.ts button recipe defines no _disabled state and a dead button advertises an affordance that never fires
2026-08-02 | Routes with no static content deleted rather than kept as stubs: /support/request, /support/confirmation, /case-status, /case/[reference], /donate/confirmation, /onboarding/[token], /campaigns/[slug], /knowledge/[slug], /events/[slug], /admin/** | Pages whose entire body was a fail-closed gate have nothing to render front-end-only; informational pages (/support, /donate, /contact, /partner, /volunteer, /complaints) were kept and stay linked
2026-08-02 | NavLink widened to NavItem = NavLink | ComingSoonNavItem, with isNavLink() as the type guard; Header/Footer branch on it and key on label | Nav entries for deleted routes must render without an href; the union keeps "has no href" unrepresentable-as-a-link at the type level rather than relying on an empty string

2026-08-07 | ActionLink gained an onDark flag for ghost CTAs on dark surfaces (white text + whiteAlpha.200 hover) | Hero "Understand PKD" used ghost navy.900 on navy.900 and was invisible until hover; global ghost recipe stays for light surfaces

2026-08-14 | Added real design primitives to theme.ts: a fluid clamp() textStyles scale (display/pageTitle/sectionTitle/cardTitle/featureTitle/eyebrow/lede/body/quote), layerStyles (card/cardInteractive/cardDark/panelTeal/panelPink/hairline), a navy-tinted shadow scale (soft/lift/float/header), duration/easing tokens, measure sizes, and globalCss text-wrap balance/pretty | theme.ts defined only colours, fonts and one button recipe, so every page re-typed its own typography inline. Three different h1 treatments had already drifted apart (PageHero 4xl->6xl/0.98/-0.04em, HomePage hero 5xl->7xl/0.92/-0.055em, HomePage h2 4xl->6xl/default). Tokens make the scale the source of truth and every existing page inherits it with no per-page edit
2026-08-14 | Extended the PublicPage kit with Ledger, StepList, FeatureCard, SplitFeature, PullQuote, StatementBand and Portrait; ContentSection gained size and width props | These patterns were hand-rolled inside HomePage.tsx and would have been re-hand-rolled on every future page. ContentSection size/width is the mechanism for vertical-rhythm variety - ten consecutive py={{16,24}} maxW="7xl" blocks were the main reason the home page read as templated
2026-08-14 | Replaced the desktop-only 650px radial "six pillars" diagram with a single responsive card grid, deleting the dashed ring, the six absolute positions, the raw rgba box-shadows and the separate stacked <ol> mobile fallback | Two implementations of one piece of content, neither shown at all widths; the absolute positions broke below lg and the raw rgba shadows bypassed the token system. Owner decision 2026-08-14
2026-08-14 | Home hero reduced from three equal-weight CTAs to one solid + one outline + a text link; the "See how the pathway works" hint became a real anchor to #the-challenge | Three peer CTAs is no hierarchy at all, and the scroll hint looked interactive but was inert text
2026-08-14 | Extracted the Button-asChild-wraps-Link composition into a single "use client" leaf, components/common/ButtonLink.tsx; ActionLink and EmptyState now compose it | Authored inside a server component, the <Link> child reaches Chakra's asChild as a React.lazy client reference, so React.Children.only throws and the page fails to prerender ("React.Children.only expected to receive a single React element child"). Confirmed by instrumenting @chakra-ui/react styled-system/factory.js: child $$typeof was Symbol(react.lazy). Keeping Button and Link in one client module guarantees a real element. Do not inline <Button asChild><Link/></Button> elsewhere
2026-08-14 | Button recipe gained defaultVariants { variant: solid, size: lg } | A size-less Button previously got no size styles at all from the recipe (EmptyState's action button had no height or padding). IconButton/CloseButton in Header now pass size="sm" px={0} explicitly to keep their 44px square targets
2026-08-14 | Home's three consecutive EmptyState blocks (campaigns, knowledge, partners) merged into one "Where things stand" section of three FeatureCards, each carrying the same status string via a new FeatureCard status prop | Three stacked "nothing here yet" panels made the last third of the page read as abandonment. All original strings are preserved verbatim, including the e2e-asserted "No verified campaigns are public yet"
2026-08-14 | Renamed public/assets/images/onyekachi.PNG to .png | next-env.d.ts declares *.png lowercase only, so the uppercase extension had no module declaration and the static import failed typecheck
2026-08-14 | ActionLink/ButtonLink/Eyebrow/TextLink/SectionHeading/SplitFeature replaced the onDark boolean with an explicit surface: "light" | "dark" | "brand" | The button recipe's action.700 text passes contrast on light surfaces only: measured 2.32:1 on navy.900 (/about hero outline CTA) and 3.67:1 on brightTeal.500 (home final CTA). A boolean could only express two of the three surfaces, and DECISIONS.log 2026-08-07 shows the same class of bug already recurring once for the ghost variant. "brand" renders navy.900 on brightTeal, which measures ~11:1
2026-08-14 | Touch targets raised to 44px on the header logo link, the header Donate button, every ButtonLink, and the skip link; eyebrow textStyle raised from 0.8125rem to 0.875rem | Measured in-browser at 390px and 1440px: logo link was 132x32, Donate 83x36, EmptyState action 263x36, skip link 149x18 — all under the 44px minimum. The 13px eyebrow was also below the 14px small-text floor
2026-08-14 | Added fluid clamp() spacing tokens (blockGap/stackGap/ctaGap/cardPad/panelPad); ContentSection now owns the heading->content gap and layerStyles carry card padding, so call sites no longer pass mt or p | Spacing was the only layer of the design system with no tokens, and drift had already appeared in the file rewritten the same day: the identical heading->content relationship was mt={{base:10,md:14}} in four sections and mt={{base:10,md:12}} in two, content->CTA was mt={12} vs mt={10}, and card padding existed at md:7, md:9 and md:10. Making the components own the gap removes the decision from the call site, exactly as textStyles did for typography
2026-08-14 | StepList switched from columns={{base:1, md:steps.length}} to a staged 1/2/3/5 ramp | Five columns from 768px gave 131px per step, about 17 characters per line of body text at bodySm — measured, not estimated. Inherited from the pre-rewrite code, which also used md:5
2026-08-14 | Founder portrait squared to 1:1 and its column narrowed; section dropped from spacious to default padding | A 4/5 portrait rendered 547x684 against a ~390px text column with alignItems=center, leaving ~250px of empty navy above the eyebrow at 1440px

2026-08-15 | Added an "About PKD" section: /pkd (what it is), /pkd/symptoms-and-causes, /pkd/diagnosis-and-treatment, with copy held as data in src/content/pkd.ts | The site asked people to navigate PKD but never explained the disease; "Learn About PKD" pointed at /knowledge, which is an empty medical-review placeholder. Copy is data for the same reason as policies.ts: this is clinical text that will be re-reviewed as a body, not edited section-by-section inside JSX
2026-08-15 | Nav group "Learn" renamed to "About PKD" and refilled (What Is PKD?, Symptoms & Causes, Diagnosis & Treatment, Knowledge Centre); Events moved from Learn to Get Involved | Keeps the header at four dropdowns instead of five — a fifth trigger crowds the lg row against the logo and Donate pill. "About" is about the organisation, "About PKD" is about the disease, and Events sits naturally beside Campaigns/Volunteer/Partner. navigation.test.ts and e2e/public.spec.ts assert the group labels and were updated with it
2026-08-15 | Added components/common/SourceNote.tsx and every PKD page carries it: named external source with an outbound link, plus the explicit statement that the page is not medically reviewed by Hope4PKD, linking /medical-disclaimer | Contract rule 8 and ADR-9: a health charity publishing clinical information must say where it came from. The Knowledge Centre's promise ("no article is labelled medically reviewed until a qualified reviewer, references and next-review date exist") applies to these pages too, so they claim no review label
2026-08-15 | Navbar restructured to the owner's specified IA: Home | About | Learn About PKD | Get Support | Get Involved | Contact | Donate. About gains Leadership & Governance; Learn About PKD splits by patient question order (Symptoms & Diagnosis, Treatment & Care) rather than by the Mayo article's own headings; Get Support gains Patient Support Process and relabels /help to Patient & Caregiver Resources; Get Involved leads with Campaigns and Volunteer | Owner decision, superseding the "About PKD" grouping I proposed earlier the same day. Still four dropdowns, so footerGroups stays five columns
2026-08-15 | /pkd routes re-cut: symptoms-and-causes -> symptoms-and-diagnosis (gains the three scans, loses causes and complications), diagnosis-and-treatment -> treatment-and-care (gains complications as "what care watches for"), causes/inheritance prose moved onto /pkd which already carried the two inherited forms | A nav label must not promise a section its page does not contain. The routes were created hours earlier and never deployed, so the rename costs no inbound links and needs no alias redirect; content/pkd.ts was unchanged, only which page renders which export
2026-08-15 | "Our Ecosystem" and "Living With PKD" omitted from the nav rather than added as comingSoon entries | Neither has an honest source: the first would name partners the site itself says are "being formalised", the second would publish lifestyle advice with no named reference (contract rule 8). comingSoon means "needs the operational service" (ADR-3b) — reusing it for "not written yet" would blur a distinction the NavItem union and navigation.test.ts enforce. Each is a one-line addition once its page exists
2026-08-15 | public/assets/images/hospital.JPG renamed to hospital.jpg and committed, mode 0600 -> 0644 | Same cause as the onyekachi.PNG rename on 2026-08-14: next/image-types/global.d.ts declares *.jpg lowercase only, so an uppercase extension has no module declaration and the static import fails typecheck. Renamed via a temp name because APFS is case-insensitive and a direct .JPG -> .jpg move is a no-op
2026-08-15 | MediaFrame gains an optional objectPosition prop defaulting to "center"; the founder-story photo uses ratio 4/5 with "50% 82%" | The source is a 1240x2208 phone portrait, so a centred cover crop in a 4/5 frame lands on the chest and cuts the head off. Extending the shared frame keeps the prefers-reduced-motion hover neutralisation in one place rather than forking a per-page variant (DESIGN_SPEC 105-109). No colour grade or scrim applied - the documentary roughness is the point on a founder story
2026-08-15 | Founder-story left rail dropped position=sticky/top rather than keeping it at a lower offset | Measured at 1440x900: with the figure added the rail is 673px and the grid is 673px, i.e. the rail is now the tallest column, so a sticky element has zero travel and never engages at any desktop width. It only appeared to work before because the rail held a heading alone (~190px) against a ~673px prose column. Keeping the declaration would be inert CSS that reads as intent
2026-08-15 | Homepage founder band switched from onyekachi.png to hospital.jpg at ratio 1 with objectPosition "50% 56%", reusing the founder-story alt text | Owner decision: the teaser and the founder-story page it links to should show the same photograph. Kept ratio 1 because the 2026-08-14 entry squared this slot deliberately to kill ~250px of empty navy. No caption, unlike the story page - navy.400 caption text would not survive tone=navy. onyekachi.png is left on disk, now unreferenced
